{"availability":"available","full":"idan-rubin/browserclaw","name":"browserclaw","description":"The AI-native browser automation library. Snapshot + ref targeting — born from OpenClaw, built for agents, by agents.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":76,"forks":7,"created":"2026-02-08T19:16:06Z","updated":"2026-10-03T20:45:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["accessibility","ai","ai-agent","browser-automation","cdp","chrome","llm","openclaw","playwright","snapshot","typescript","web-scraping"],"demo":"https://browserclaw.org/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:42.338Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:42.338Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:42.338Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:42.338Z","stars":76,"forks":7}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The browser tool, not the agent. You bring the brain.","The AI-native browser automation library — born from OpenClaw, built on Playwright, embeddable in any TS/Node agent loop. Snapshot + ref targeting: no CSS selectors, no XPath, no vision model — just numbered refs that map to interactive elements.","Most other tools in this space ship a complete AI agent: they take your task, own the LLM loop, decide what to click, and click it. Great — until you already have an agent. Then you've got two brains fighting over who's in charge."],"features":["Deterministic — refs resolve through Playwright locators and bound DOM identities, one ref → one element. No coordinate guessing, no LLM re-interpreting targets between calls.","Cheap & fast — a text snapshot is a fraction of the tokens of a screenshot, and there's no vision API round-trip in the targeting loop.","Reliable — built on Playwright's auto-wait and locator engine, not homegrown DOM poking.","Yours to compose — no framework opinions, no agent loop, no hosted platform. Drop it into whatever architecture you already have."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/idan-rubin/browserclaw/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8e0062ff5539f6a47480b6d7b4c7c83c9e1ef0a973de73c8057b353c943ad52d","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:42.432Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:42.432Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The browser tool, not the agent. You bring the brain.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/idan-rubin/browserclaw/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Stagehand — Accessibility tree + natural language primitives (page.act(\"click login\")).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/idan-rubin/browserclaw/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"For a stable, shared profile across runs (persistent login state, preserved history), omit isolated and use profileName / userDataDir instead.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/idan-rubin/browserclaw/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"8e0062ff5539f6a47480b6d7b4c7c83c9e1ef0a973de73c8057b353c943ad52d","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/idan-rubin/browserclaw/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:42.433Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-03T20:45:50Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/idan-rubin/browserclaw/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:42.435Z","hash":"8e0062ff5539f6a47480b6d7b4c7c83c9e1ef0a973de73c8057b353c943ad52d","originalBytes":42271,"storedBytes":42271,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["await","const","ref","true","browserclaw","typescript","page","text","snapshot","browser","playwright","default","refs","chrome","tab","click","url","when","false","agent","type","cdp","name","page.click","page.waitfor","actions","clear","isolated","role","tree","element","fill","interactive","only","profile","wait","before","console.log","directory","done","launch","link","navigation","one","resolves","run","same","selector","set","upload","after","api","body","call","custom","examples","file","import","llm","network